GITHUB PUSH TRACKING LOG

For anyone viewing this file for the first time:

This text file is used only as a personal tracking system for GitHub pushes. Each time I make a new push to GitHub, I update the number in this file in sequence:

1
2
3
4
5
6
7
...and so on.

The purpose is simply to help me keep track of each push and confirm that my latest changes successfully made it into the GitHub repository.

For example, if I change the number in this file from 4 to 5 before making a push, I can check the GitHub repository afterward. If GitHub shows the updated number 5, I know that the newest version of this file—and the changes included with that push—reached the repository.

IMPORTANT:

This file has absolutely no effect on the website, application, database, server, or source code functionality.

It is not a configuration file.
It is not required by the application.
It is not used by Node.js, Express, EJS, SQLite, Render, or GitHub.

It is simply a personal GitHub push tracking log used for organization and verification.

